WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.360
Your AI isn't stupid, it's blind.

2
00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:07.080
Most agent memory is a pile of raw text with a search box on top.

3
00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:11.200
But the decisions that matter are often somewhere it can't see.

4
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.280
I spent the last year building memory for company-scale

5
00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:18.080
agents, and the fix isn't storing more.

6
00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:21.440
It's distilling knowledge, tracking changes, and keeping

7
00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:24.440
permissions intact once the source is gone.

8
00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:25.640
You get that right,

9
00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:28.320
and an unremarkable local model gets

10
00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:30.680
99% of frontier quality.

11
00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:36.760
I'm Ran Aroussi. I wrote yfinance, I run VarOps, and at AI DevCon in New York,

12
00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:39.480
I'll show you exactly how we build it.

13
00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:40.440
So register at

14
00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:44.000
aidevcon.io, and I'll see you there.
